WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 012, en. Timings estimated from the script.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.385
<v the Bute estate office clerk>Counterpart lease, sixth of November, eighteen seventy-seven. The Bute Trustees to John Williams, builder, of System Street, Roath. A plot in Clyde Street. Into the Roath box.

2
00:00:10.735 --> 00:00:18.042
<v the Bute estate office clerk>Now the Trustees' abstract of receipts and payments for the year. Every pound in, every pound out, written fair.

3
00:00:22.392 --> 00:00:30.469
<v The Grandson>The statement of Mary (Nancy) Williams, typed around nineteen seventy-four. She writes that in eighteen seventy-seven Bute served notice to quit.

4
00:00:30.819 --> 00:00:38.896
<v Nia>That reaches us through her statement, as the Legal Wiki's Master Timeline records it. We haven't seen any notice paper itself.

5
00:00:39.246 --> 00:00:50.015
<v The Grandson>Then a sale. The farmhouse, the buildings and about ten acres to Daniel Thomas, with about nine acres kept by Bute. The original deed and plan are missing.

6
00:00:50.365 --> 00:01:08.827
<v Nia>The catalogue links this family-identified plan image to an eighteen seventy-seven agreement between Bute and Daniel Thomas and Son. We don't hold the agreement. Sale, or a quarry lease of the house parcel? Terms, the plan's standing, any reverter, whether the deed survives outside family papers: all open.

7
00:01:09.177 --> 00:01:21.869
<v Nia>So, the money. Bute X.6(12), the Trustees' abstract for eighteen seventy-seven. The Case Analysis calls it the decisive test: a capital receipt means sale, rent alone means lease, and perhaps a court order.

8
00:01:22.219 --> 00:01:24.019
<v The Grandson>And we have it?

9
00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:30.908
<v Nia>Not obtained, not transcribed. And an account book alone wouldn't settle the legal nature or the extent.

10
00:01:31.258 --> 00:01:36.258
<v The Grandson>Last of all: a lease dated sixth November eighteen seventy-seven, to John Williams.

11
00:01:36.608 --> 00:01:46.223
<v Nia>No matching Llandough deed found. DBDT/79/1 was checked: second of May eighteen seventy-seven, Pembroke Terrace, Cardiff. Other similarly named Cardiff leases are catalogue leads only.

12
00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.881
<v The Grandson>This one's even the right day.

13
00:01:49.231 --> 00:01:59.231
<v Nia>Same date, Bute Trustees, a John Williams. But a builder of System Street, Roath, for a plot in Clyde Street. Photographed and excluded. Not the farm.

14
00:01:59.581 --> 00:02:13.812
<v Nia>So the November lease stays unlocated. Without it there's no boundary, no transfer to the Williamses, no route to a Cedwyn Estate. Parties, property, plan, rent, term, and its link to the Thomas quarrying are all unknown.

15
00:02:14.162 --> 00:02:16.469
<v The Grandson>Then we keep asking Bute's papers.

16
00:02:16.819 --> 00:02:18.619
<v Nia>Box by box.
